  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge2Knowledge Entrepreneurship curriculum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project focuses on entrepreneurship development at a pivotal time during the development of youth in their societies, namely when they are being educated. In this phase of their life, being exposed to the right information and practical assignments can be a life-changing experience. It will give them a chance to gauge the merits of entrepreneurship for themselves and gives them the tools and insights to successfully start and grow their business after graduating, if they choose to do so.Prior to this curriculum development Knowledge-to-Knowledge project, a needs assessment was executed to ascertain the challenges and ambitions of the participating knowledge institutes (KI). During the project at hand a context and KI-specific entrepreneurship curriculum will be identified with all stakeholders involved. It will also mark the beginning of a subsequent capacity building, curriculum development and accreditation process that will engrain these valuable tools and findings in the KIs, the students, and through the Ministry of Higher Education into the society at large. The KIs from Angola will form a Community of Practice so that lessons learnt and experiences can be shared and potential future projects and collaborations can be sparked.</narrative>
  </description>
